  "prefLabel": "Odb 407.05 Replacement of Private Water Supply",
  "priorExpiration": "2019-09-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Odb 407.05 Replacement of Private Water Supply.\n\n(a) An owner of a private water supply may request reimbursement under RSA 146-D:6 I for the installation of a new or replacement groundwater supply well and appurtenances.\n\n(b) A new or replacement private water supply shall be approvable if connection to a public or non-public water supply system is not available, or if the cost of connection would exceed the cost of establishing a viable new or replacement private water supply.\n\n(c) Installations of private groundwater supply wells shall be approved based on conformance with technical criteria established in Env-Dw 300 or We 600, We 700 and We 800 of the water well board, as applicable.\n\n(d) Reimbursable costs shall include site location and development activities, construction of the supply well and pump installation, treatment systems, piping installations, plumbing connections and other necessary appurtenances, startup costs, and the costs required to abandon a contaminated supply well.\n\nSource. #8491, eff 11-22-05; ss by #9935-A, eff 9-1-11, EXPIRED: 9-1-19\n\nNew. #12942, eff 12-15-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/odb100-600.html"
